Alert Summary:
A critical command injection vulnerability was exploited on a Palo Alto Networks firewall. The attacker injected OS commands via a malicious HTTP cookie targeting the GlobalProtect login portal.

Indicators:

• Source IP: 144.172.79.92 (10 detections on VirusTotal)
• Destination IP: 172.16.17.139
• Hostname: PA-Firewall-01
• CVE: CVE-2024-3400
• HTTP Method: POST
• Requested URL: /global-protect/login.esp
• Cookie: path traversal + curl command to port 4444 + whoami
• Device Action: Allowed

Analysis:
The attacker sent a crafted POST request to the GlobalProtect login portal injecting OS commands inside the cookie field. Commands included path traversal, a curl request to an external IP on port 4444 indicating a reverse shell attempt, and whoami to identity system privileges. Source IP had 10 malicious detections on VirusTotal. Log Management showed 4 connection events from the attacker IP. Terminal
History showed no executed commands suggesting the exploit was detected before full execution. No pentest authorization found in email records.
Verdict: True Positive - Attack partially mitigated

Recommended Actions:
Patch PA-Firewall-01 against CVE-2024-3400, block IP 144.172.79.92, monitor port 4444 for reverse shell attempts.